            "type": "progress",
            "createdAt": 1774677382449,
            "message": "Implementation complete. Here's what was built:\n\n## Order Management API (`/api/orders`)\n| Endpoint | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /api/orders` | Create order with multi-platform source, line items, shipping address |\n| `GET /api/orders/:id` | Get order details by ID |\n| `GET /api/orders` | List with filters: platform, status, date range, pagination |\n| `PUT /api/orders/:id/status` | Update status via state machine (pending→confirmed→processing→shipped→delivered) |\n\n## Inventory Sync API (`/api/inventory`)\n| Endpoint | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `GET /api/inventory/sync` | Trigger multi-platform sync (Amazon/Shopify/TikTok Shop) |\n| `GET /api/inventory/:sku` | Query SKU stock levels |\n| `PUT /api/inventory/:sku` | Update quantity (with Redis distributed lock) |\n\n## Key design decisions:\n- **Distributed locks** on inventory writes to prevent overselling\n- **State machine** for order status — invalid transitions return 409\n- **Multi-currency** support (USD/CNY/EUR/JPY) with JPY integer rounding\n- **Zod validation** on all inputs\n- **Conservative sync** strategy: takes minimum across platforms\n- **PostgreSQL JSONB** for flexible nested data (line items, addresses, platform quantities)\n\nThe sandbox couldn't install some devDependencies (typescript/tsx/zod), but the code is ready to run with `npm install && npx tsx src/index.ts` in a standard environment. Handing off to QA for test case development.",
